  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「パチョリ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%91%E3%83%81%E3%83%A7%E3%83%AA",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 108886331,
      "text": "パチョリ とは、シソ科ミズトラノオ属の植物である。ハーブの一つであり、主に精油（パチョリ油）に加工され利用される。古くから香や香水に用いられている。インド原産。その名前はタミル語で緑の葉を意味するパッチャイ・イライ に由来する。パチュリ、パチュリーとも。漢方ではパチョリの全草を乾燥させたものを霍香（カッコウ）と呼び霍香正気散などの漢方薬に用いる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Patchouli」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patchouli",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1373080566,
      "text": "Patchouli is a species of flowering plant in the family Lamiaceae, commonly called the mint or deadnettle family. The plant grows as a bushy perennial herb, with erect stems reaching up to 75 centimetres (30 in) in height and bearing small, pale, pink-white flowers."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Patchouli」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patchouli#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1373080566,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Patchouli grows well in warm to tropical climates. It thrives in hot, humid weather but not extended periods of direct sunlight. If the plant withers due to lack of water, it tends to recover quickly after rain or watering. Although rare, the seed-producing flowers are very fragrant and blossom in late autumn. The tiny seeds may be harvested for planting, but they are very delicate and easily crushed. Cuttings and grafts from the mother plant and subsequent rooting in loamy soil are the most common methods for propagation.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
